  "summary": "A post-DEF CON X DM phishing campaign lures security researchers to a real Google Doc with a container-bound Apps Script sidebar that fakes a decryption failure and ClickFix instructions, beacons victim IP/geolocation/wallet presence to the actor's Telegram, and routes macOS and Windows users down separate malware chains. macOS victims receive an AMOS infostealer variant via a piped zsh command or a signed-out DMG download, while Windows victims receive a ClickOnce app, an encoded PowerShell loader, and three encrypted payloads (NetSupport Manager RMM, a stolen-Lenovo-signed local proxy that installs a self-generated CA, and a Ledger wallet implant).",
